{"questions":[{"question_id":"1l17otb3e","paperTitle":"JEE Advanced 2014 Paper 2 Offline","year":2014,"examDate":2014,"subject":"chemistry","chapter":"basics-of-organic-chemistry","chapterGroup":"organic-chemistry","topic":"isomerism","type":"mcq","marks":3,"negMarks":1,"permalink":"pisomers-of-hexane-based-on-their-branching-can-be-divid-jee-advanced-chemistry-some-basic-concepts-of-chemistry-yxru4dkh1cve1irn","content":"<p>Isomers of hexane, based on their branching, can be divided into three distinct classes as shown in the figure.</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l17z24g9/3125aa02-3dfb-44a0-82db-79de7ef30122/6c75e6a0-ad14-11ec-abb2-4983f0354b7b/file-1l17z24ga.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1l17z24g9/3125aa02-3dfb-44a0-82db-79de7ef30122/6c75e6a0-ad14-11ec-abb2-4983f0354b7b/file-1l17z24ga.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0px auto;max-height:40vh\" alt=\"JEE Advanced 2014 Paper 2 Offline Chemistry - Basics of Organic Chemistry Question 24 English\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1l17z24g9/3125aa02-3dfb-44a0-82db-79de7ef30122/6c75e6a0-ad14-11ec-abb2-4983f0354b7b/file-1l17z24ga.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1l17z24g9/3125aa02-3dfb-44a0-82db-79de7ef30122/6c75e6a0-ad14-11ec-abb2-4983f0354b7b/file-1l17z24ga.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l17z24g9/3125aa02-3dfb-44a0-82db-79de7ef30122/6c75e6a0-ad14-11ec-abb2-4983f0354b7b/file-1l17z24ga.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/1l17z24g9/3125aa02-3dfb-44a0-82db-79de7ef30122/6c75e6a0-ad14-11ec-abb2-4983f0354b7b/file-1l17z24ga.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/1l17z24g9/3125aa02-3dfb-44a0-82db-79de7ef30122/6c75e6a0-ad14-11ec-abb2-4983f0354b7b/file-1l17z24ga.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/1l17z24g9/3125aa02-3dfb-44a0-82db-79de7ef30122/6c75e6a0-ad14-11ec-abb2-4983f0354b7b/file-1l17z24ga.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\"></p>\n<p>The correct order of their boiling point is</p>","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"I > II > III"},{"identifier":"B","content":"III > II > I"},{"identifier":"C","content":"II > III > I"},{"identifier":"D","content":"III > I > III"}],"correct_options":["B"],"explanation":"<p>As the branching increases, the boiling point decreases. This is because the van der Waals forces of attraction decrease.</p>"}]}